1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Opening a position in TestingView

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Draw a Long Position on the chart.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This becomes your trade template.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,539
Open its settings to define risk.

5
00:00:12,619 --> 00:00:15,819
Risk can be a percentage of your account…

6
00:00:15,819 --> 00:00:21,800
…or a fixed cash amount, like $500.

7
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:25,719
When it reaches the entry line, the trade is on.

8
00:00:25,719 --> 00:00:30,199
The trade appears instantly in the journal below.

9
00:00:30,199 --> 00:00:33,359
See live entry, stop, target, and PnL.

10
00:00:33,359 --> 00:00:38,339
You can also track run-up and drawdown, along with many other info that are customizable.

11
00:00:38,339 --> 00:00:43,259
Click the camera icon to save a snapshot.

12
00:00:43,259 --> 00:00:45,240
Want break-even protection?

13
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,060
Click the small circle next to the trade.

14
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,740
A BE line appears—
drag it anywhere you want.

15
00:00:49,899 --> 00:00:53,219
When price touches it,
SL moves to entry.

16
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:57,039
Now the trade is at break-even risk.

17
00:00:57,039 --> 00:01:01,519
Take another snapshot at this stage.

18
00:01:01,519 --> 00:01:04,179
Keep replaying…

19
00:01:04,179 --> 00:01:08,500
Entry was tapped again, so closing at 0.

20
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:12,500
Take a final snapshot to mark the exit.

21
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:17,000
Add notes for the trade in the journal.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:27,599
Then open the viewer
and review all 3 snapshots.
